<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - March 25.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - March 25.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF MARCH 25 VERSUS MARCH 18, 1997		   DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA   10/9     0/2     312/332   43/8    365/351    222</p>
<p> SASK.	0/1     0/0	59/68    11/0     70/69	23</p>
<p> B.C.	 0/0     0/1	44/57     0/0     44/58	19</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 2/2	4/4	6/6	  2</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 1/1	0/0	1/1	  0</p>
<p> TOTAL     10/10    0/3     418/460   58/12   486/485    266</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
